Subject: [PATCH] AN7581: make the borrowed SCU syscon adapter unloadable

The AN7581 SCU adapter only caches syscon regmaps and reads the SRAM size.
It owns no IRQ, mapping, clock, reset or asynchronous work. Its exported
symbol consumers pin the module while loaded, but the missing exit handler
made it permanent even after all consumers had unloaded.

Provide an AN7581-only exit handler that drops the cached aliases. The
syscon providers retain ownership of their regmaps; do not release or write
them. Keep the other SoCs' legacy resource lifecycle unchanged.

--- a/bsp/core/ecnt_scu.c
+++ b/bsp/core/ecnt_scu.c
@@ -1298,6 +1298,16 @@ static int ECNT_SCU_DRV_PROBE(void)
 	/* Keep clock/reset ownership and the PBus timeout IRQ with their drivers. */
 	return 0;
 }
+
+static void __exit an7581_scu_exit(void)
+{
+	/* Exported-symbol users pin this module. These maps belong to syscon. */
+	an7581_np_scu = NULL;
+	an7581_chip_scu = NULL;
+	l2c_sram_size = 0;
+}
+module_exit(an7581_scu_exit);
+
 #else
 static void pbus_timeout_init(void)
 {
